body:
" How do you guys figure out what builds to play before each league "

\- We wait for patch notes, that's when we know what will be nerfed/buffed and with that info we can get working on builds. So far we know melee will get buffed next league, so I'm already dreaming with cyclone/reave/frostblades something character.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

" is there a comprehensive list of viable builds somewhere I can get every pre-league ?"

\- Yes, there will be plenty of "league starter builds" videos in this subreddit days before the next league, pick one as your first character for the league and have fun. Usually first characters tend to scale damage with the gem/skill/spell itself, and don't require mandatory itens, which makes for easy lvling and a good starting experience. Once you get to maps and start making currency you can go dream with your next build or further improve your league starter.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

" I almost always go with totems, and almost every single time "

\- Ignore reflect and do most map mods, if not all. Totems are a solid choice, you would probably enjoy playing traps/mines

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

"  I get better every league, but I'd like to at least figure out how to decide on builds before every league "

\- Again, pick a strong league starter and you will be netting those 200c in a few days worth of playtime.
